---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getAllGyms } from '../lib/gyms.js';

const gyms = getAllGyms();
const unpriced = gyms.filter((g) => !g.has_price);

const title = 'For gym owners — Austin Gym Prices';
const description =
  'How to correct your gym’s pricing on Austin Gym Prices, and what we will and will not do with your listing.';

const correctHref =
  'mailto:reports@austingymprices.com?subject=Listing%20correction%20%E2%80%94%20%5Byour%20gym%20name%5D';
const hello = 'mailto:hello@austingymprices.com';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/for-gym-owners">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">All gyms</a> / For gym owners</nav>
    <h1>For gym owners</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      If your gym is listed here, this page explains where the numbers came from, how to
      correct them, and what we will not do.
    </p>

    <h2>Your price is wrong. Fix it.</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={correctHref}>reports@austingymprices.com</a> with your gym name and
      the correct figures. The useful ones are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Monthly rate for a standard adult membership</li>
      <li>Enrollment or initiation fee, and any annual fee</li>
      <li>Contract length, or month-to-month</li>
      <li>Day pass price, if you sell one</li>
      <li>Anything that changes what a member actually pays — a fee charged on a delay, a
        different billing cycle, a minimum term</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A link to the page on your own site showing the rates is the fastest possible
      correction, because that is exactly what we read.
    </p>

    <h2>Where your listing came from</h2>
    <p>
      From your own public pricing page, or from asking. Nothing here is bought, scraped
      from a competitor, or estimated from national averages. Every gym page shows the
      date its price was last checked and the domain it was read from.
    </p>
    <p>
      {unpriced.length} of the {gyms.length} gyms listed have no price shown at all,
      because we could not source one. If that is yours, it is not a judgement — it means
      we have nothing we can stand behind, and one email fixes it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    <ul>
      {/* Promise the INVARIANT, not the absence. "We will never take a referral
          fee" is a promise about our business model that a future us might
          have to break; "money never moves a price or a ranking" is a promise
          about the product, and it is the one that actually protects the
          reader. Stating an absence we may not keep is worse than stating a
          rule we will. */}
      <li><b>Sell placement in results.</b> No gym can pay to rank higher, appear more
        prominently in comparisons, or have a competitor excluded. Ranking is by price
        and nothing else — that will never change.</li>
      <li><b>Compromise the data.</b> Prices come from your own published rates or
        direct confirmation. No payment alters a listed price, a fee disclosure, or a
        known-for line.</li>
      <li><b>Editorialise.</b> We state fees plainly, including the awkward ones, but we
        do not editorialise about them. &ldquo;Charged 75 days after signup&rdquo; is a
        fact worth stating; &ldquo;watch out for this trap&rdquo; is not our line.</li>
      <li><b>Publish reviews or ratings.</b> Other sites do that. This one is about price.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="owner-tools">
      We&rsquo;re building tools for gym owners — for updates, email
      <a href="mailto:hello@austingymprices.com">hello@austingymprices.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Can I remove my gym?</h2>
    <p>
      Membership pricing that a business publishes on its own website is public
      information, and comparing it is the point of the site. But if something here is
      wrong, misleading or out of date, that is a real problem and we want to fix it
      quickly — email <a href={correctHref}>reports@austingymprices.com</a> and it gets
      dealt with.
    </p>

    <h2>Is there an owner portal?</h2>
    <p>
      Not yet. Managing your own listing — updating rates directly, adding photos and
      amenities — is planned. For now there is no login and no form on this site at all;
      corrections come by email and a person makes the change.
    </p>

    <h2>Anything else</h2>
    <p>
      General enquiries: <a href={hello}>hello@austingymprices.com</a>. More on sourcing
      and update frequency in the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .wrap {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 34px 28px 90px;
  }

  .crumb {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }

  .crumb a {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .crumb a:hover {
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 2.8rem);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.02;
  }

  .lede {
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 40px 0 10px;
  }

  p {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0 0 14px 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
</style>
